## Comparative Analysis

### Paper Under Review
The paper proposes a learnable three-channel codec inspired by the Gray-Wyner network to disentangle common and task-specific information for multiple vision tasks. It proves non-trivial theoretical bounds (Theorem 1: linking lossy Gács-Körner and Wyner common information via interaction information; Theorem 2: deriving a practical Lagrangian objective). Experiments span synthetic data, colored MNIST, and vision benchmarks (Cityscapes, COCO), consistently outperforming independent coding baselines.

### Calibration Comparison

| Paper | Score | Key Comparison |
