## Comparative Analysis

**Paper being scored: CCAT (Classifier-Constrained Alternating Training)**

### Dimension-by-Dimension Comparison

| Dimension | CCAT | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Novelty** | Moderate-to-Good | Bridging class↔modality imbalance via frozen classifier is a genuine novel insight; individual components (LoRA, alternating training) are pre-existing |
| **Technical soundness** | Good | Gradient dynamics analysis is clear and supports the core claim; secondary update step is heuristic but functional |
| **Empirical support** | Good | +6.76% on KS is substantial; clean ablations isolate each component; t-SNE evidence for feature discriminability |
| **Significance** | Moderate | Multimodal imbalance is a recognized problem, but scope is limited to 2 modalities on 3 small/standard benchmarks |
