**Empirical support (weak):** This is the paper's most significant weakness. Evaluation is on a single small model (DeepSeek R1 Qwen-1.5B). The faithfulness metric is arguably circular/unvalidated. The only baseline is a "naive RL" strawman—no comparison against contrastive training, length-penalized RL, or human-written short solutions. No ablations on the prior model's strength. DeepCritic (4.7) and LRT (5.0), despite having issues, tested across multiple models and benchmarks. RLKV (4.5) evaluated two model families and four benchmarks.

**Significance (moderate-high):** CoT faithfulness is a genuinely important safety problem. The framing as a sparse reward / data-densification problem is useful to the community. On significance, this is comparable to DeepCritic (4.7) and LRT (5.0).

