### VideoJudge vs. Calibration Papers

**Dimensions of comparison:**

| Dimension | VideoJudge | DeepCritic (4.7) | W2S-VQA (3.3) | GAIA2 (8.0) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Novelty | Solid – first bootstrapped video judge framework | Solid – deliberate critique pipeline | Moderate – W2S for VQA | High – new benchmark paradigm + ARE framework |
| Technical soundness | Partial – circularity in 2/4 benchmarks, calibration flaws | Partial – limited domain scope | Moderate – confounded by model capacity | High – comprehensive evaluation |
| Empirical support | Moderate – independent benchmarks positive but partial | Good – state-of-the-art on multiple math benchmarks | Moderate – missing ablations | Very strong – large-scale, diverse agents |
| Significance | Moderate – fills a real gap in video evaluation | Moderate-high – scalable oversight |  Moderate | High – advances agent evaluation |
