The OSR paper is a genuine contribution that fills an important research gap with comprehensive experiments and a novel failure mode discovery. Its main weaknesses—lack of statistical validation for large-scale results and partly speculative causal mechanism—are significant but not fatal; they are typical revision targets. The paper sits comfortably above all reject-range calibration papers and is comparable to TRANSFIR (6.0) and slightly below LAMDA (6.7). The absence of variance estimates for the central claims (which the paper itself argues are the critical takeaway) is the primary reason it does not reach the level of LAMDA or Scaling with Collapse. A score in the 5.6–6.2 range is appropriate.

