The paper's core contribution is real and fills an important gap, but the methodological weaknesses — particularly the prompt inconsistency that undermines the "real-world" claim and the lack of annotation transparency — push it into borderline reject territory for ICLR. More comparable to the answerset consistency paper (4.0) but slightly above it due to the practical relevance and breadth of model evaluation.

