The current paper sits above the 6.7-tier papers (better empirical breadth and dual contribution), but below the 8.0 paper (which solved a truly long-standing open problem with complete theoretical machinery). It aligns most closely with the 7.5-range (ReLU geometry), with slightly weaker specialization trade-offs but stronger practical relevance. The missing statistical validation and sample-size analysis are real gaps but not fatal — they are addressable in revision and do not undermine the core contributions.

