**vs. LBF-NPE (score 6.7):** Novel parameterization with theoretical convexity guarantees and good experiments. SCaSML has a more impactful core idea (inference-time scaling for PDE solving) and stronger empirical validation across more problem settings. SCaSML is comparable or slightly stronger.

**vs. Differentiable Contact (score 5.5):** Novel theoretical framework (4 properties) with empirical validation but missing statistical robustness. SCaSML has stronger statistical validation and broader experimental coverage. SCaSML is clearly stronger.

**vs. MOSIV (score 5.0):** Good systems paper but with significant gaps (no real-world validation, no direct parameter evaluation). SCaSML has better theoretical foundations and more thorough experimental validation. SCaSML is clearly stronger.

**vs. Operator Flow Matching (score 4.0):** Missing ablations, no statistical validation, incomplete baselines. SCaSML is substantially stronger in every dimension.

