WeCAN sits between the 5.5-6.0 range papers. It has genuine novelty (WeCA layer + theoretical analysis), strong empirical gains, and good generalization results. However, the lack of code, the disconnect between skip action theory and main experiments, and the dense presentation keep it from reaching 6.5+. It's slightly stronger than the contact model (5.5) and comparable to TRANSFIR/HiGS (6.0), but the weaknesses (especially no code and the skip-action disconnect) pull it slightly below those.

