The paper sits between the 6.0 and 7.0 calibration points. It has stronger practical impact than the 6.0 paper (evolution/compression) but less theoretical depth than the 7.0 paper (attention heads). The weaknesses (c_dec validation is correlational, heuristic interpretation of the metric, preliminary automatic tuning) are real but don't fundamentally undermine the contribution.

I'd place this paper at approximately **6.3**: solidly above borderline accept territory due to its clear, actionable findings and practical tool, but below the 7.0 level due to the gap between toy model demonstrations and LLM validation, and the preliminary nature of the practical solution.

